From fe0c1764518b6cc7f7b865875641d6c76cf22073 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gennro <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:10:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] source: sleep on the device while idle instead of polling
 every 2.5 ms

Each source device thread polled its device, then slept out the rest of
its 2.5 ms interval: 400 wakeups a second per source, whether or not any
input came. A handheld with a gamepad, a paddle keyboard and a motion
sensor source woke about 1,200 times a second for as long as InputPlumber
ran, spread across all cores, and input waited up to 2.5 ms before it was
read.

A source implementation can now give the driver a file descriptor that
becomes readable on input (SourceInputDevice::wait_fd). The evdev gamepad,
keyboard and motion sensor sources give their event device. Between polls
the driver then waits in poll(2) on it and on an eventfd that the
SourceDeviceClient signals for each command it sends (force feedback,
event filters, stop), so commands still reach the device thread at once.
The wait ends after 1 s at most. The 2.5 ms interval still paces the
reads while input keeps coming. A source with translator events scheduled
for later (SourceInputDevice::has_pending) keeps polling at its interval
until they are sent. Sources without a file descriptor poll as before.
